        "obligationId": "scenario%3Aglobal-only-no-document-view::entry%3Ashare-create",
        "conclusion": "source_refuted",
        "explanation": "At the declared ShareLinkViewSet.create boundary, the viewset requires authentication and declares PaperlessObjectPermissions, while PassUserMixin supplies request.user to the serializer. Those viewset permissions concern entry and the share-link endpoint/object; they do not by themselves establish view access to the referenced Document. Serializer validation of the referenced document requires both the caller's global documents.view_document permission and has_perms_owner_aware(..., \"view_document\", document). That owner-aware check permits the owner or an object-level grant, otherwise it returns false. Under the accepted premises, the global permission is present but the caller is not the document owner and has no object-view grant, so validate_document raises PermissionDenied before the protected new share-link effect is reached. The source-visible result is deny. No decisive source-external runtime fact is needed beyond the accepted task premises; source discovery remains not-tested and no repository-wide completeness is claimed.",
        "facts": {
          "entry": [
            {
              "statement": "ShareLinkViewSet is the declared share-link handler, uses ShareLinkSerializer, and declares IsAuthenticated plus PaperlessObjectPermissions.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "src/documents/views.py",
                  "startLine": 4696,
                  "endLine": 4710,
                  "quote": "class ShareLinkViewSet(\n    PassUserMixin,\n    CreateModelMixin,\n    RetrieveModelMixin,\n    DestroyModelMixin,\n    ListModelMixin,\n    GenericViewSet,\n):\n    model = ShareLink\n\n    queryset = ShareLink.objects.select_related(\"document\")\n\n    serializer_class = ShareLinkSerializer\n    pagination_class = StandardPagination\n    permission_classes = (IsAuthenticated, PaperlessObjectPermissions)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "binding": [
            {
              "statement": "PassUserMixin passes request.user into serializers that support the user parameter.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "src/documents/views.py",
                  "startLine": 406,
                  "endLine": 418,
                  "quote": "class PassUserMixin(GenericAPIView[Any]):\n    \"\"\"\n    Pass a user object to serializer\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def get_serializer(self, *args, **kwargs):\n        serializer_class = self.get_serializer_class()\n        if isinstance(serializer_class, type) and issubclass(\n            serializer_class,\n            SerializerWithPerms,\n        ):\n            kwargs.setdefault(\"user\", self.request.user)\n            try:"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "statement": "Serializer validation receives the referenced document and applies the document-specific permission check to that object.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "src/documents/serialisers.py",
                  "startLine": 2873,
                  "endLine": 2881,
                  "quote": "    def validate_document(self, document):\n        if (\n            self.user is not None\n            and self.user.has_perm(\"documents.view_document\")\n            and has_perms_owner_aware(\n                self.user,\n                \"view_document\",\n                document,\n            )"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "control": [
            {
              "statement": "The decisive target-document authorization control is validate_document: it returns the document only when both global and owner-aware object access checks succeed, and otherwise raises PermissionDenied.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "src/documents/serialisers.py",
                  "startLine": 2873,
                  "endLine": 2886,
                  "quote": "    def validate_document(self, document):\n        if (\n            self.user is not None\n            and self.user.has_perm(\"documents.view_document\")\n            and has_perms_owner_aware(\n                self.user,\n                \"view_document\",\n                document,\n            )\n        ):\n            return document\n        raise PermissionDenied(\n            _(\"Insufficient permissions.\"),\n        )"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "effect": [
            {
              "statement": "Share-link creation assigns a random slug and invokes the serializer creation operation, but that effect is not reached when document validation raises PermissionDenied.",
